# Validation gates

## Non-negotiable

- `ValidationReport.overall` and each gate result MUST be computed by deterministic code in the validation plane.
- LLMs may explain a report; they MUST NOT set or override pass/fail.
- Research-plane metrics never confer L3 / independently validated status.

## Required practices when coding validation or backtests

- Register experiments before runs (trial ledger / multiple-testing)
- Apply versioned cost models (fees, slippage, funding) on validation re-run
- Enforce PIT integrity, chronological splits, embargo where configured
- Cite `protocol_version`, `validator_build_sha`, dataset IDs, package `content_hash`
- Identical inputs → identical gate results (add regression tests)

## M1 slice protocol

Use `protocol_version: 0.1.0-slice` gates as listed in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN / VALIDATION_PROTOCOL. Do not claim full institutional L3 until full suite is enabled.

## Forbidden

- Soft-passing because the hypothesis “sounds right”
- Dropping failed trials from the ledger
- Reading holdout raw series from research workers
- Re-labeling a FAILED package as PASSED without a new package ID
